<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine congress body okays excise tax bill.</title>
<headline>Philippine congress body okays excise tax bill.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The bicameral conference committee of the Philippine Congress approved on late Wednesday night the shift to a specific tax scheme on beer and cigarettes that would raise additional yearly revenues of 6.0 to 6.5 billion pesos, Senator Juan Ponce Enrile said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The approved version of the bill is a victory for the administration of President Fidel Ramos who had pushed for the scrapping of the ad valorem tax which had provided opportunities for tax evasion.</p>
</text>
